/**
 * Browser management — CDP Chrome lifecycle for the extractor.
 *
 * Lifecycle:
 *
 *   1. A fresh CLI run starts its own Browser Tools Chrome.
 *      It does not attach to another agent's existing browser on :9222.
 *      Browser Tools auto-allocates a separate port when :9222 is busy.
 *
 *   2. On disconnect, call scripts/stop.mjs to kill just our Chrome (PID-based).
 *      → scripts/stop.mjs only kills the PID it recorded — never touches main Chrome.
 *      → Optionally call scripts/stop.mjs --clean to delete the profile copy.
 *
 * Block recovery (resetChrome()):
 *   Stops Chrome, re-syncs a fresh copy of the profile (clears tainted cookies),
 *   then starts a new Chrome instance and reconnects. Callers get a clean session.
 */

